{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Asymptotics","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.Asymptotics","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Monoid.WithTop","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Basic","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.StandardPart"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.preceq_algebraMap_mul_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.preceq_algebraMap_mul_left","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Asymptotics.lean#L160-L164","doc":"Rescaling by a nonzero real preserves the Big-O class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.preceq_of_prec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.preceq_of_prec","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Asymptotics.lean#L156-L158","doc":"`≺` refines `≼`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.preceq_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.preceq_trans","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Asymptotics.lean#L150-L154","doc":"`≼` is transitive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.preceq_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.preceq_refl","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Asymptotics.lean#L147-L148","doc":"`≼` is reflexive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.prec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.prec","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Asymptotics.lean#L143-L145","doc":"**Surreal little-o** relation: `x ≺ y` iff `Ow x < Ow y`.\nEquivalent under the bridge to classical `x = o(y)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.preceq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.preceq","kind":"def","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Asymptotics.lean#L139-L141","doc":"**Surreal Big-O** relation: `x ≼ y` iff `Ow x ≤ Ow y`.\nEquivalent under the Hahn bridge to classical `x = O(y)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.Ow_algebraMap_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.Ow_algebraMap_mul","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Asymptotics.lean#L131-L131","doc":"Rescaling by a nonzero real leaves the leading exponent\nunchanged (finite nonzero reals have `Ow = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.Ow_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.Ow_mul","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Asymptotics.lean#L128-L128","doc":"Multiplication is valuation-additive: `Ow (x·y) = Ow x + Ow y`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.Ow_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.Ow_zero","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Asymptotics.lean#L126-L126","doc":"Zero has order `⊤`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.Ow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.Ow","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Asymptotics.lean#L124-L124","doc":"The ω-adic order, valued in `WithTop Γ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder.mk","kind":"ctor","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Asymptotics.lean#L120-L120","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.OmegaOrder","kind":"class","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/Asymptotics.lean#L80-L132","doc":"A commutative `ℝ`-algebra `K` admits an **ω-adic order** with\nexponents in `Γ`: the leading exponent in Conway normal form,\nvalued in `WithTop Γ`.\n\nClassical analogue is the p-adic order `ord_p`.  Under the QOU\nnotational convention, the symbol is typeset as `$O_\\omega$`\n(Big-O register) because the equivalence\n`f = O(g) ⟺ Ow(f) ≤ Ow(g)` makes Big-O the natural reading.\n\n## Why the exponent group is a separate parameter\n\nUntil 2026-08-16 this class fixed `Ow : K → WithTop K` and required\n`[SurrealField K]`.  Exponents-in-`K` is right for `𝐍𝐨`, which is\nclosed under `ω`-exponentiation — but it is a *self-referential*\nstructure, and it made the class **uninstantiable**: it left `Ow`\nwith no model anywhere in this tree, so every `[OmegaOrder]`-\nconditional result was untested for satisfiability.  See bean\n`qou-x20w`, and `qou-ffwk` for the carrier-hygiene work that\nsurfaced it.\n\nTwo changes fix that, both conservative:\n\n* exponents move to their own `Γ`, matching the standard shape of a\n  leading-exponent valuation (and Mathlib's\n  `HahnSeries.orderTop : HahnSeries Γ R → WithTop Γ`); take\n  `Γ := K` to recover the old reading for `𝐍𝐨`;\n* the base weakens from `[SurrealField K]` to a commutative ring\n  with an algebra over an arbitrary scalar ring `S`, which is all\n  `Ow_algebraMap_mul` ever used.  It was previously phrased with\n  `SurrealField.ofReal`; nothing about a leading-exponent valuation\n  needs the scalars to be the reals, and leaving them abstract also\n  keeps this module clear of the §7c mixed-regime rule (a generic\n  base ring beside a real-field type is exactly what that rule\n  forbids).  Surreal callers instantiate `S := ℝ`, since every\n  `SurrealField` is canonically a real algebra via\n  `SurrealField.toAlgebra` with `algebraMap` equal to `ofReal`.\n\nTogether these admit the Hahn model in `HahnOmegaOrder.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}